Title: Test suite writes to production beat-outcomes.jsonl — isolate log path
Created: 2026-05-14
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-14T07:10Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

`OUTCOMES_LOG` in `beat.py` is hardcoded to
`~/.claude/logs/beat-outcomes.jsonl`. The test suite runs beat.py against
fake project paths (names like `test_pick_ticket_uses_project_0`,
`test_closed_then_idle_returns_0`, etc.) and writes their phase-outcome
records directly into this production log.

After 7 days, beat-outcomes.jsonl contains 100–200 entries per test project
(30+ fake projects), dwarfing the real entries and skewing every analysis
that reads the file (nightbeat-report, nightbeat-supervisor-survey,
permission-prune telemetry).

The root cause: `_record_phase_outcome` uses the module-level `OUTCOMES_LOG`
constant, which resolves at import time to the real path. Tests that call
`beat.main()` or its sub-functions inherit this path with no way to override it.

## Actions

1. In `beat.py`, make `OUTCOMES_LOG` overridable via environment variable:
   ```python
   OUTCOMES_LOG: Path = Path(
       os.environ.get("BEAT_OUTCOMES_LOG") or
       str(HARNESS_DIR / "logs" / "beat-outcomes.jsonl")
   )
   ```
2. In `tests/test_beat.py`, set `BEAT_OUTCOMES_LOG` to a `tmp_path`-scoped
   file in every test fixture that invokes beat code:
   ```python
   @pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
   def isolate_outcomes_log(tmp_path, monkeypatch):
       monkeypatch.setenv("BEAT_OUTCOMES_LOG", str(tmp_path / "outcomes.jsonl"))
   ```
3. Apply the same isolation to `LOGDIR` / `COUNTER_FILE` if tests write there.
4. Optionally: backfill by pruning `test_*` entries from the production log
   (one-off script — not required for exit criteria).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `BEAT_OUTCOMES_LOG` env var overrides the log path in beat.py
- [ ] All test fixtures that invoke beat functions use a tmp_path-isolated log
- [ ] Running `pytest tests/` does not append any new `test_*` entries to
      `~/.claude/logs/beat-outcomes.jsonl`
- [ ] `make check` passes
